WEBVTT

00:00.800 --> 00:04.520
Okay, employees,
start by introducing yourselves.

00:05.500 --> 00:09.150
I'm Tsuruga Ami!
High school second-year, karate club!

00:09.150 --> 00:10.230
Yah!

00:11.010 --> 00:13.740
Tsukishima Riho. University second-year.

00:13.740 --> 00:14.820
Glad to be here.

00:15.560 --> 00:17.340
Ono Shiragiku.

00:17.340 --> 00:20.660
I'm a university second-year, like Riho-san.

00:21.430 --> 00:23.100
Hououji Akane.

00:23.950 --> 00:25.880
Age 19. Job hopper.

00:26.690 --> 00:27.960
Makuzawa Ouka.

00:28.410 --> 00:31.090
Age 19. Tech school student.

00:31.780 --> 00:35.970
Will these girls be the goddesses
that save this café,

00:36.800 --> 00:38.220
or...

00:39.080 --> 00:41.610
So, since we'll all be living here together,

00:41.610 --> 00:43.730
we need to divide up the chores—

00:43.730 --> 00:47.860
No way! If I do any cooking,
my acrylic nails will come off!

00:47.860 --> 00:52.110
My specialty is getting stuff dirty,
so I don't do laundry!

00:52.110 --> 00:55.450
I have low blood pressure,
so I can't get up early.

00:55.450 --> 00:58.700
Oh, uh... I...

01:00.450 --> 01:03.500
I hate cleaning. Don't wanna.

01:07.060 --> 01:09.500
Will you quit complaining already?!

01:10.080 --> 01:14.570
I swear... These girls aren't goddesses
of fortune or<i> devils of poverty.</i>

01:14.570 --> 01:16.200
They're jinxes!

01:33.070 --> 01:35.650
The Café Terrace and Its Goddesses

02:48.490 --> 02:50.110
If we're gonna live in the same house,

02:48.600 --> 02:53.190
Episode 2: "A Promise with Grandma"

02:50.110 --> 02:52.410
obviously we're gonna share the chores!

02:52.410 --> 02:55.150
What else is there, Filth Specialist?!

02:55.150 --> 02:59.820
Well, I mean, Grandma
did all of it for us until now!

02:59.820 --> 03:00.730
Huh?

03:00.730 --> 03:02.910
She cooked for us every day.

03:02.910 --> 03:05.660
And she did all the laundry and cleaning.

03:06.080 --> 03:09.790
And she didn't gripe at us
like Hayato-kun does.

03:09.790 --> 03:12.590
For real. Talk about
a huge difference, right?

03:12.590 --> 03:14.000
Uh...

03:14.300 --> 03:16.800
I sure would love some of Grandma's curry...

03:16.800 --> 03:19.390
Yeah, you always ate three full plates of it!

03:19.390 --> 03:22.330
Oh, and when Ami-chan's with her club...

03:22.330 --> 03:22.840
Hey!

03:23.570 --> 03:28.140
Did you ever think that maybe you're the
ones who sent Grandma to an early grave?

03:29.850 --> 03:32.760
O-Of course it wasn't us!

03:32.760 --> 03:34.670
We did help sometimes.

03:34.670 --> 03:37.240
Yeah! Like with tidying up
the café and stuff!

03:37.240 --> 03:39.240
We did the dishes, too!

03:39.240 --> 03:41.240
That's what you were <i>supposed</i> to do!

03:41.520 --> 03:44.080
Pay us a part-time wage, then, Master.

03:44.080 --> 03:44.780
Yeah!

03:44.780 --> 03:45.720
Get real!

03:45.720 --> 03:47.080
U-Um...

03:47.410 --> 03:49.520
I'll do it.

03:49.520 --> 03:53.040
I like cooking, and I don't
particularly hate cleaning.

03:53.390 --> 03:54.960
Shiragiku, was it?

03:54.960 --> 03:55.980
Y-Yes...

03:55.980 --> 03:58.880
Use "-san"! You're younger
than her, you know!

03:59.230 --> 04:01.360
I hate unequal treatment,

04:01.360 --> 04:04.640
and I hate people who read the room and
try to play the good guy even more.

04:05.890 --> 04:07.950
Of course, what I hate most of all

04:07.950 --> 04:11.310
is people who shove
all the work onto the timid one

04:11.310 --> 04:13.760
so they get off easy themselves.

04:13.760 --> 04:16.140
I didn't say I <i>wouldn't</i> do it!

04:16.140 --> 04:18.190
Oh, really?

04:18.490 --> 04:20.700
Okay, then, we'll start
by cleaning the house!

04:20.700 --> 04:22.880
Once that's done, we'll do the café!

04:22.880 --> 04:24.360
Fine.

04:24.670 --> 04:26.870
Jeez, what the heck?

04:27.920 --> 04:29.370
This is such a pain!

04:29.810 --> 04:30.870
Quick draw!

04:30.870 --> 04:32.250
Take that!

04:32.250 --> 04:34.300
And how do you like this?!

04:34.300 --> 04:35.620
Quit playing around!

04:36.930 --> 04:38.360
Hey, hold it!

04:39.270 --> 04:41.880
Take that!

04:39.680 --> 04:41.400
S-Stop!

04:44.420 --> 04:45.430
Get moving!

04:46.290 --> 04:47.340
For crying out loud...

04:47.700 --> 04:51.020
Why do I have to scrub the floor, too?

04:51.020 --> 04:53.710
The stairs were particularly dirty.

04:54.060 --> 04:55.800
So be thorough.

04:56.600 --> 04:58.000
I get it, okay?!

04:58.000 --> 04:59.570
Why don't you do something, too?

04:59.570 --> 05:02.690
Oh, shut up. I'm about to do the laund—

05:07.010 --> 05:08.570
Ouka-chan!

05:08.570 --> 05:10.630
Your panties are showing.

05:25.480 --> 05:26.930
I think he's dead.

05:27.360 --> 05:29.680
Hmph! He <i>should</i> be!

05:30.470 --> 05:31.930
That idiot.

05:32.650 --> 05:35.770
Did she have to kick me right in the face?

05:37.680 --> 05:38.900
What's this?

05:39.260 --> 05:43.030
Hey, my laundry's already drying.

05:43.030 --> 05:44.480
Could you save yours for—

05:44.480 --> 05:47.820
Oh, you mean these?
I'll hang them out while I'm at it.

05:49.690 --> 05:52.160
No!

05:50.340 --> 05:52.590
What's with you?!

05:52.590 --> 05:53.360
What's going on?

05:53.360 --> 05:54.080
What is it?

05:54.080 --> 05:55.410
Th-This jerk...

05:55.410 --> 05:58.040
He opened the laundry net my underwear was in

05:58.040 --> 05:59.720
and took my stuff out of it!

06:00.290 --> 06:03.000
What? I can't hang it out otherwise.

06:03.000 --> 06:04.670
What's wrong with opening it?

06:04.670 --> 06:07.970
Everything's wrong!
Put them back in right now!

06:07.970 --> 06:10.860
What's your deal?
You got something dangerous in here?

06:10.860 --> 06:11.930
Don't look in it!

06:11.930 --> 06:13.550
Gross.

06:13.550 --> 06:14.960
Scum!

06:14.960 --> 06:16.990
Yeah, that <i>is</i> pretty creepy.

06:16.990 --> 06:18.440
Hayacchi...

06:18.780 --> 06:22.020
Seriously, what's the big deal?
It's just underwear!

06:22.020 --> 06:23.640
"Just" underwear?

06:27.440 --> 06:31.830
I... I apologize.
I'll be more thoughtful in future.

06:32.570 --> 06:35.600
You can clean the café
on your own as punishment.

06:35.600 --> 06:36.660
Huh?!

06:37.100 --> 06:38.370
What?

06:39.270 --> 06:43.840
I swear, those girls are so damn selfish!

06:44.220 --> 06:47.360
Ow, my back...

06:47.360 --> 06:49.400
That should just about do it.

06:56.050 --> 06:58.180
That coffee mill is so old-fashioned.

06:59.090 --> 07:01.690
Shouldn't you buy a new one?

07:01.690 --> 07:04.060
Don't be silly.

07:04.060 --> 07:08.710
This manufacturer's coffee mills
produce the best-tasting grounds.

07:09.760 --> 07:12.360
It's my favorite mill.

07:15.110 --> 07:16.540
No choice, I guess.

07:17.090 --> 07:18.440
I'll clean this, too...

07:18.440 --> 07:21.080
Excuse me, that coffee mill...

07:21.080 --> 07:24.330
It was really important to Grandma,

07:24.330 --> 07:27.500
so please don't be too rough with it.

07:27.500 --> 07:28.840
I know.

07:29.130 --> 07:31.430
She made me clean it up all the time.

07:31.430 --> 07:34.680
Oh, right... I guess she would have.

07:35.040 --> 07:38.430
Um, thank you for what you said this morning.

07:38.430 --> 07:39.530
Huh?

07:39.530 --> 07:42.190
My university term is starting soon,

07:42.190 --> 07:47.650
so I knew it would be difficult
if I had to do all the cleaning alone.

07:48.080 --> 07:52.700
Oh, pardon me! I know you didn't
say it for my sake, of course!

07:53.320 --> 07:54.910
Why do you try to be so polite?

07:54.910 --> 07:55.950
Huh?

07:55.950 --> 07:58.840
We're family, aren't we?
As far as the old hag was concerned...

07:58.840 --> 08:01.580
Do you speak that politely to your family?

08:01.580 --> 08:04.170
Oh... R-Right...

08:04.170 --> 08:07.670
You're right... I mean, yeah! We <i>are</i> family!

08:07.950 --> 08:10.840
Oh, I came to let you know dinner's ready.

08:10.840 --> 08:12.380
Come eat with us!

08:12.380 --> 08:14.860
Oh, you guys can go ahead.

08:14.860 --> 08:15.790
I'll stay here and—

08:15.790 --> 08:17.010
You can't!

08:17.290 --> 08:20.070
We all have to eat our meals together!

08:21.730 --> 08:25.230
Oh, did you finish
cleaning the café, pervert?

08:25.230 --> 08:27.660
You think you're gonna eat with us, pervert?

08:27.660 --> 08:28.810
Shut up!

08:28.810 --> 08:32.030
C'mon, don't be mean to him.

08:32.320 --> 08:33.950
We're family, yeah?

08:34.420 --> 08:37.700
What's this? What's gotten
into you, Kiku-chan?

08:38.120 --> 08:41.160
N-Not a thing... I mean, nothing!

08:41.160 --> 08:42.620
Nah, you're acting weird.

08:42.620 --> 08:44.040
You dropped the polite tone.

08:44.040 --> 08:45.290
Hey, guys!

08:46.800 --> 08:48.680
Look, look!

08:51.270 --> 08:53.980
The cherry tree in the garden
is blooming already?

08:53.980 --> 08:55.390
It's so pretty!

08:55.390 --> 08:57.260
It really is!

08:57.970 --> 09:00.260
We have front-row seats for flower viewing!

09:00.620 --> 09:04.140
True. Drinking while we look
at the blossoms at night sounds nice.

09:04.140 --> 09:06.860
You're still underage, Akane-chan.

09:06.860 --> 09:09.020
Come on, let's eat already!

09:11.080 --> 09:13.400
Let's eat!

09:13.400 --> 09:15.130
This looks great!

09:13.400 --> 09:15.130
It's piping hot.

09:15.130 --> 09:17.020
Looks amazing!

09:15.980 --> 09:17.500
Where should I start?

09:19.320 --> 09:21.240
Hmm... Guess I'll start with this!

09:21.680 --> 09:24.600
We all have to eat our meals together!

09:24.600 --> 09:26.460
Huh? Why?

09:26.980 --> 09:30.460
It was the one promise we made with Grandma!

09:30.840 --> 09:34.910
That we'd always eat our meals
together, as a family.

09:34.910 --> 09:36.860
Everyone eat lots, okay?

09:38.640 --> 09:40.220
Family, huh?

09:41.700 --> 09:45.080
I'm kind of impressed she managed to get
so many problem children together.

09:56.640 --> 09:59.070
Wh-Why are <i>you</i> in there?!

09:59.070 --> 10:03.180
W-Well, I mean, the pigtailed chick
told me to use the bath first!

10:04.200 --> 10:07.580
You should've put up the
"bath in use" sign, then!

10:07.580 --> 10:10.600
N-Nobody told me you had
a system like that here!

10:10.600 --> 10:11.820
Hayacchi...

10:14.900 --> 10:17.920
Hang on! I haven't done anything!

10:17.920 --> 10:21.800
World peace, and all the girls in this house,

10:21.800 --> 10:23.910
are under my protection!

10:25.810 --> 10:31.810
The Right Way to Speak Informally

10:26.140 --> 10:28.760
The Right Way to Speak Informally!

10:29.190 --> 10:32.190
We all have to eat our meals together!

10:32.730 --> 10:36.190
Oh... I-It isn't that I'm angry or anything.

10:36.190 --> 10:40.360
Uh, I mean... I'm not...
mad or nothin', ya get me?

10:40.360 --> 10:42.570
Oh, I'm terribly sorry!
That was Kansai dialect...

10:42.570 --> 10:45.950
Whoops! That correction was too polite!

10:45.950 --> 10:47.260
Uh, too darn polite?

10:47.260 --> 10:49.630
Ain't it? Innit? Ya dig?!

10:49.630 --> 10:51.370
Just stick with being polite, okay?

10:53.620 --> 10:55.230
A pre-opening?

10:55.230 --> 10:55.920
Yeah.

10:56.240 --> 10:58.510
It'd be too risky to fully open
right off the bat,

10:58.510 --> 11:01.480
so I've decided to practice with you guys.

11:01.930 --> 11:06.680
Cooking aside, as the owner,
I gotta at least be able to make coffee.

11:06.680 --> 11:09.430
Okay, Shiragiku, you can play the server.

11:09.430 --> 11:10.330
R-Right.

11:10.330 --> 11:12.190
Use "-san," would you?!

11:12.560 --> 11:15.320
I bet you've never even
worked part-time before.

11:15.320 --> 11:17.190
So you're not gonna cook?

11:17.190 --> 11:20.200
The coffee's definitely gonna be gross.

11:21.540 --> 11:23.000
Try not to be too shocked.

11:23.370 --> 11:28.150
I watched Grandma make coffee all the time.

11:31.310 --> 11:34.460
I'll serve you the best cup you've ever had.

11:39.140 --> 11:42.280
Huh... He actually looks like
he knows what he's doing.

11:42.700 --> 11:45.140
Hayacchi! You're looking like a master!

11:45.140 --> 11:46.180
Shut up!

11:48.280 --> 11:49.680
Thank you for waiting.

11:49.680 --> 11:51.360
Your blend coffee.

11:51.360 --> 11:53.690
Do we really need someone to play the server?

11:53.690 --> 11:55.020
Did you know?

11:55.020 --> 11:58.910
The aroma of coffee beans changes
depending on where they're from,

11:58.910 --> 12:00.940
and the taste depends on how you grind them.

12:01.520 --> 12:05.700
We do pour-over coffee with a paper drip
filter, so we generally use a medium grind,

12:05.700 --> 12:07.640
but when making espresso...

12:07.640 --> 12:08.490
Yuck.

12:08.490 --> 12:09.330
Huh?

12:09.630 --> 12:11.370
It just tastes weak.

12:11.370 --> 12:12.910
It has no flavor, either.

12:12.910 --> 12:14.540
It's just bitter.

12:15.040 --> 12:16.720
That can't be right...

12:16.720 --> 12:19.050
I know! You're just being mean to me!

12:19.360 --> 12:23.550
Your pride will never allow you
to say that any coffee I made is good!

12:25.050 --> 12:28.810
There's no way we can sell this stuff,

12:29.210 --> 12:33.060
dear erudite study-bug café owner
who makes lousy coffee.

12:34.570 --> 12:37.060
What?!

12:39.400 --> 12:41.280
Thanks for dinner!

12:41.630 --> 12:45.370
You made us another great
meal today, Shiragiku-san.

12:45.370 --> 12:46.280
Thanks.

12:46.620 --> 12:49.150
Hey, do you know where Hayato-kun is?

12:49.150 --> 12:51.690
He disappeared right after dinner.

12:51.690 --> 12:56.040
He said he'd be in the café
practicing making coffee.

13:00.790 --> 13:02.970
Damn it, this is all wrong.

13:03.440 --> 13:07.680
It does seem to taste
weaker than Grandma's.

13:08.170 --> 13:12.580
...dear erudite study-bug café owner
who makes lousy coffee.

13:14.840 --> 13:18.810
Whoa, too close! Remembering
what that blonde chick said

13:18.810 --> 13:21.630
almost made me black out from sheer rage.

13:21.630 --> 13:24.530
You just keep talking, don't you?

13:24.970 --> 13:27.180
I can't focus with all the noise.

13:27.180 --> 13:29.530
H-How long have you been there?!

13:30.360 --> 13:32.330
About an hour.

13:33.840 --> 13:35.690
She's a real piece of work.

13:35.690 --> 13:38.920
She sat there listening to me
talk to myself all that time?

13:42.720 --> 13:44.030
What's this for?

13:44.030 --> 13:47.480
I'm getting cold,
so I'm gonna get a cup of coffee.

13:47.480 --> 13:48.800
This isn't enough!

13:49.310 --> 13:51.560
I deducted the service fee.

13:52.160 --> 13:56.810
You know, the way you dissed my coffee
was pretty damn condescending.

13:56.810 --> 14:00.980
How about you make a cup for me, then?

14:02.150 --> 14:05.220
I think you mean, "Please make me a cup."

14:05.810 --> 14:07.820
Okay! I don't want one anymore!

14:10.430 --> 14:11.660
Here.

14:13.440 --> 14:15.120
I just said I didn't want it.

14:15.120 --> 14:16.660
Leave it, then.

14:16.660 --> 14:18.250
That'd be a waste!

14:18.250 --> 14:19.620
Drink it, then.

14:20.130 --> 14:22.490
Seriously, she's a real piece of work.

14:28.530 --> 14:29.930
This flavor...

14:34.940 --> 14:39.210
Did Grandma teach you how to make coffee?

14:43.170 --> 14:44.770
What if she did?

14:45.470 --> 14:49.530
Then teach me. I never
actually learned it from her.

14:54.200 --> 14:56.950
P-Please teach me.

14:59.750 --> 15:01.950
He's so much trouble, really.

15:01.950 --> 15:05.420
He sulks whenever something
doesn't go his way.

15:05.420 --> 15:09.250
Even though he always ends up
being the one to apologize.

15:09.250 --> 15:10.710
But you know...

15:11.640 --> 15:16.710
When he does that, his face just looks so...

15:18.690 --> 15:21.300
You look so cute right now, Hayato.

15:25.610 --> 15:29.070
Ugh, forget it! Don't make fun of me!

15:32.390 --> 15:35.190
Okay, sorry. I'll teach you.

15:36.710 --> 15:42.340
It would look pretty bad if the café's
waitress had to make the coffee, wouldn't it?

15:44.260 --> 15:46.980
Come on. I'll teach you.

15:47.750 --> 15:50.310
Damn it, she's messing with me!

15:51.950 --> 15:55.100
You look pretty cute yourself, when you smile.

15:55.100 --> 15:58.700
I like you better that way
than when you try to look all cool.

15:58.700 --> 16:00.810
Oh, yeah, <i>super</i> cute!

16:01.750 --> 16:03.830
Yeah? Thanks.

16:05.080 --> 16:06.730
Damn it! I shouldn't have tried!

16:06.730 --> 16:08.230
Blush or something!

16:09.760 --> 16:11.340
I see.

16:11.340 --> 16:15.240
So the longer you let it bloom,
the richer it tastes.

16:21.840 --> 16:25.020
You look pretty cute yourself, when you smile.

16:28.630 --> 16:33.520
Wh-What the hell?!
I put the "bath in use" sign up!

16:33.520 --> 16:35.760
Hayacchi...

16:36.290 --> 16:38.010
Whoa, wait, wait, wait!

16:42.480 --> 16:46.660
It's so hot. I should've made it iced coffee.

16:49.940 --> 16:53.860
Why do I have to do
the courtesy visits with you?

16:53.860 --> 16:55.690
Quit complaining.

16:55.690 --> 16:59.910
We have to let our business partners
know we're reopening, right?

17:01.210 --> 17:02.410
Oh?

17:02.410 --> 17:04.430
Could it be...

17:04.430 --> 17:06.880
that you actually wanted
to go on a date with me?

17:06.880 --> 17:08.410
Process of elimination.

17:08.410 --> 17:09.000
Huh?

17:09.460 --> 17:11.710
Akane's attitude and expression
aren't the best.

17:12.090 --> 17:14.590
Shiragiku is too shy and reserved.

17:14.590 --> 17:18.800
Ouka's constant badmouthing of me
would hurt the café's reputation.

17:18.800 --> 17:22.520
And Ami is just an idiot,
so there's no way I'd bring her.

17:23.560 --> 17:26.020
Well, I guess bringing Ami-chan
<i>would</i> be risky.

17:26.020 --> 17:29.900
Yeah, so it's not like I'm expecting
anything out of you.

17:29.900 --> 17:32.350
I just need you to show me where to go.

17:32.350 --> 17:33.570
Oh, really?

17:33.840 --> 17:36.610
Well, do your best, then.

17:37.220 --> 17:41.260
Oh, really? You're opening up Familia again?

17:41.260 --> 17:43.560
I'm sure your grandma's overjoyed.

17:43.560 --> 17:45.620
Maybe. I wouldn't know.

17:45.900 --> 17:48.250
All I ever heard her do was complain.

17:48.250 --> 17:52.160
Nah, she was always thinking about you.

17:52.160 --> 17:53.300
I see.

17:54.820 --> 17:56.350
Uh...

17:56.350 --> 17:59.970
I'm sorry! I think he's a little nervous!

18:00.250 --> 18:04.330
He's honestly a terrible owner who
doesn't know anything about our café.

18:04.330 --> 18:07.230
I hope you can help teach him the ropes!

18:07.230 --> 18:10.840
Familia wouldn't exist
without this roasting plant!

18:10.840 --> 18:14.230
All right! I'll give you
a special low price for a while!

18:15.320 --> 18:16.860
Thank you so much!

18:16.860 --> 18:20.460
Well, your grandma did do a lot for us.

18:21.430 --> 18:24.330
We've decided to reopen the café.

18:24.330 --> 18:25.830
I hope we can count on you again.

18:26.120 --> 18:28.990
Dear me! Is that you, Hayato-kun?

18:28.990 --> 18:31.120
You've grown!

18:31.120 --> 18:32.200
Uh-huh...

18:32.900 --> 18:34.840
That's right!

18:34.840 --> 18:39.120
There's no way a café run by an antisocial
greenhorn like him can succeed!

18:39.120 --> 18:41.640
So please, at least supply us
with tasty vegetables, okay?

18:41.640 --> 18:44.140
All right! When I get a good, fresh one in,

18:44.140 --> 18:45.870
I'll let you know right away!

18:45.870 --> 18:48.890
Thank you! I love you, mister!

18:49.230 --> 18:52.560
Come on! You need to talk to him, too!

18:52.560 --> 18:55.530
I swear, he's so useless!

18:57.490 --> 19:00.860
Damn it! What's her deal?

19:00.860 --> 19:04.070
She's making me look like
a loser everywhere we go!

19:05.810 --> 19:07.980
Anyway, that's all of them, right?

19:07.980 --> 19:11.330
It sure took long enough,
since you never stop talking.

19:11.330 --> 19:12.560
We're not done.

19:12.560 --> 19:13.530
Huh?

19:13.530 --> 19:14.940
One more stop.

19:23.570 --> 19:24.720
Look...

19:24.720 --> 19:26.170
Be quiet a sec.

19:27.810 --> 19:30.250
I came here to report to the gods.

19:32.310 --> 19:35.160
Grandma always said that
when we start something new,

19:35.160 --> 19:40.230
we should tell the gods about it
at the local shrine.

19:40.860 --> 19:42.030
Well, who knew?

19:42.030 --> 19:45.620
As ditzy as you act, you're
conscientious about that, at least.

19:46.480 --> 19:48.620
And what's <i>your</i> deal?

19:48.960 --> 19:51.400
Weren't we supposed to be
making courtesy visits?

19:51.400 --> 19:54.220
Huh? That's what we just did.

19:54.220 --> 19:57.840
What, standing there with a sulky look
and saying, "We're reopening"?

19:58.560 --> 20:00.880
That's what you call a courtesy visit?

20:02.650 --> 20:04.970
I made a joke out of it because
people were watching,

20:04.970 --> 20:07.510
but running your own business isn't easy!

20:07.510 --> 20:10.640
The world doesn't revolve
around you, you know!

20:11.000 --> 20:15.130
It's proper manners to show respect to
the people who'll be helping you, isn't it?!

20:15.900 --> 20:19.020
If you're asking for a favor, the least
you can do is bow your head!

20:20.320 --> 20:23.240
When you said you were
reopening Grandma's café,

20:23.240 --> 20:25.530
I wondered how strong
your resolve really was.

20:26.000 --> 20:27.680
And I'm disappointed.

20:27.680 --> 20:32.150
With you running the place, we'll be
shutting down again within a year.

20:33.700 --> 20:35.250
The resolve to run that café,

20:36.250 --> 20:38.880
and the resolve to keep it going...

20:39.660 --> 20:42.410
Grandma had that.

20:47.140 --> 20:50.790
You're right. My resolve
wasn't actually that strong.

20:51.690 --> 20:55.400
But it's not as if I want to run
the café into the ground.

20:57.890 --> 20:59.650
I'll be more careful from now on.

21:00.360 --> 21:04.390
Oh... really? Well, as long as you get it.

21:06.390 --> 21:09.260
I mean, it was your first time, so...

21:10.780 --> 21:11.910
You're leaving?

21:12.520 --> 21:15.120
I'm going to talk to all of them
one more time.

21:15.890 --> 21:17.720
And this time, I'll bow like I should.

21:27.040 --> 21:29.420
Hayato-kun!

21:31.870 --> 21:33.960
An apology for being too hard on you.

21:34.700 --> 21:37.240
No one's around, so you can look.

21:38.160 --> 21:39.480
A free peek at a college girl's...

21:40.030 --> 21:42.480
p-a-n-t-i-e-s.

21:42.940 --> 21:44.490
A-Are you nuts?!

21:44.490 --> 21:45.740
What are you—

21:49.570 --> 21:52.390
H-Hayato-kun...

22:00.540 --> 22:01.500
FORTUNE

22:00.540 --> 22:01.500
EXCELLENT LUCK

22:02.480 --> 22:04.570
Hayato-kun, huh?

22:04.570 --> 22:08.130
He's not very reliable,
as a boss or as a man.

22:08.130 --> 22:12.060
The one you're waiting
for will come to you
Romance will develop
from a connection at work
No concerns of sickness
Find fortune in an
unexpected place when
moving to a new home

22:08.690 --> 22:11.340
Looks like my fortune was way off the mark.

23:42.020 --> 23:57.030
Episode 3: "Opening"

23:42.610 --> 23:45.020
How'd you like that peek
at a college girl's panties?

23:45.020 --> 23:46.760
Are you girls actually nymphos?

23:46.760 --> 23:47.500
What?!

23:47.500 --> 23:48.820
I thought it seemed weird.

23:48.820 --> 23:52.540
You're all constantly making me look at
your underwear and naked bodies!

23:52.540 --> 23:55.070
We're not! The only nympho is Kiku-chan!

23:55.070 --> 23:57.030
Huh?! What do you mean?!
